1
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:10,761
[player 1] ♪ Ready or not, here I come ♪

2
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:18,143
[player 2] ♪ Ready or not, here I come ♪

3
00:00:18,977 --> 00:00:22,856
[player 3] ♪ Ready or not, here I come ♪

4
00:00:24,191 --> 00:00:25,984
TAG
A GAME WHERE ONE CHASES AND CATCHES OTHERS

5
00:00:26,068 --> 00:00:28,737
[player 1] We used to play tag
all the time as kids.

6
00:00:29,529 --> 00:00:32,115
[player 2] I was always the one
who caught everyone.

7
00:00:32,199 --> 00:00:33,659
Hey, Eunsil.

8
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:35,410
You can't use wrestling on me!

9
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:36,995
Wait, this is cheating.

10
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:38,747
[player 3 laughing playfully]

11
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:42,876
This is fun.

12
00:00:45,045 --> 00:00:47,881
But this is about survival.

13
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:49,633
[player 4] I'm so pissed off.

14
00:00:49,716 --> 00:00:50,801
[player 5] The Seeker's playing us.

15
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:52,010
[player 6] It's just us.
Why can't you talk?

16
00:00:52,094 --> 00:00:53,720
[screams] Please!

17
00:00:53,804 --> 00:00:56,014
[player 7] You can't trust
these damn people.

18
00:00:56,098 --> 00:00:58,016
-[player 8] Are you the Seeker?
-[player 9] Something's off.

19
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,894
-[player 10] Something's off.
-[player 11] I can't trust anyone. Damn.

20
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:02,854
[Pani Bottle] Damn it. Fuck.

21
00:01:02,938 --> 00:01:03,939
Fuck!

22
00:01:04,523 --> 00:01:06,525
A GAME OF TAG

23
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:07,693
DEADLY TAG

24
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:11,405
AN ELIMINATION GAME
WHERE ONLY THE LAST PERSON STANDING WINS

25
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:14,324
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

26
00:01:27,671 --> 00:01:29,256
[player 1 sighs]

27
00:01:35,012 --> 00:01:37,889
[host] Welcome to the "Deadly Tag."

28
00:01:39,224 --> 00:01:40,851
The rules here are simple.

29
00:01:41,852 --> 00:01:43,979
You either chase or be chased.

30
00:01:44,688 --> 00:01:47,733
All your abilities
will become the ultimate power

31
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:49,735
that lets you dominate the food chain.

32
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:53,155
Do whatever it takes.

33
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:57,284
Team up when it serves you best,

34
00:01:57,993 --> 00:01:59,870
make the most calculated betrayals,

35
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:04,207
and fight your way
to the top of the food chain.

36
00:02:06,168 --> 00:02:07,961
PARK JIMIN, BRAINS & POLITICS
ANNOUNCER

37
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:11,548
ZZONE, POLITICS
SINGER

38
00:02:12,799 --> 00:02:14,217
GYEONG SUJIN, PHYSICAL
ACTRESS

39
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,101
[Jimin] Wait, they're all women.

40
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:26,688
This might actually be doable.

41
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:30,275
Based on appearances alone,
they were all women.

42
00:02:30,359 --> 00:02:33,445
I started thinking about
how I could beat them.

43
00:02:33,528 --> 00:02:36,907
PANI BOTTLE, POLITICS
CONTENT CREATOR, TOP TRAVEL YOUTUBER

44
00:02:41,328 --> 00:02:43,955
SHIN JIEUN, PHYSICAL
TEAM KOREA BEACH VOLLEYBALL PLAYER

45
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:49,711
YOUN SANGHYUN, PHYSICAL & BRAINS
ACTOR, THEATER MAJOR

46
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:52,547
[Sanghyun] I took off my blindfold

47
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:54,841
and saw a woman behind me.

48
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,552
I thought, "This could work."

49
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:00,931
JANG EUNSIL, PHYSICAL
OLYMPIC WRESTLER, PHYSICAL: ASIA WINNER

50
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,433
KIM DDOLDDOL, POLITICS & BRAINS
CONTENT CREATOR, ENGINEERING GRADUATE

51
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:06,395
[Ddolddol] I'd never been
blindfolded before.

52
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:09,856
They locked me up, tied me down,
and wouldn't let me move.

53
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,108
Maybe I shouldn't have come.

54
00:03:12,192 --> 00:03:14,861
LEE JOONSU, PHYSICAL
COLLEGE STUDENT, THEATER MAJOR

55
00:03:15,487 --> 00:03:18,782
HORSEKING, PHYSICAL
FITNESS CONTENT CREATOR, BUSINESS MAJOR

56
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:21,326
HWANG JAEGYUN, PHYSICAL
RETIRED BASEBALL PLAYER

57
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:24,329
[Jaegyun] I saw something written in red
in front of me.

58
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:31,461
I tried hard to figure it out,
but I couldn't wrap my head around it.

59
00:03:32,045 --> 00:03:35,632
[Horseking] When I turned around,
I noticed we were chained together.

60
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:38,218
I thought I needed to free myself first.
But then...

61
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:39,970
-[loud explosion]
-Geez!

62
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:41,054
[Horseking] What the heck?

63
00:03:41,138 --> 00:03:44,349
-[explosion]
-[screams]

64
00:03:45,225 --> 00:03:48,395
[host] The first game begins now.

65
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,648
[multiple explosions]

66
00:03:56,862 --> 00:03:59,489
-[Horseking] What the heck?
-[players screaming]

67
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,746
The rules are simple.

68
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:10,250
Use any strategy and do whatever it takes

69
00:04:10,333 --> 00:04:14,337
to escape the room
and race to the finish line.

70
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:15,922
You have 10 minutes.

71
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:22,554
The last person to arrive
becomes the first elimination candidate.

72
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:23,972
DEADLY TAG
RESTRICTED AREA

73
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:26,057
[♪ low, tense music playing]

74
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:28,894
[Ddolddol] I had to get out of there.

75
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,395
The fire was blazing.

76
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:31,563
Things were blowing up.

77
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:33,690
I was really starting to panic.

78
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:35,859
[Dail] When I felt the heat from the fire,

79
00:04:35,942 --> 00:04:37,652
I was stunned.

80
00:04:37,736 --> 00:04:39,988
YANG DAIL, POLITICS & PHYSICAL
SINGER

81
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:43,116
When I took off the sack,
I saw the box in front of me.

82
00:04:43,658 --> 00:04:45,410
CLUE BOXES PLACED BEFORE THE PLAYERS

83
00:04:45,494 --> 00:04:47,037
I knew I had to get to that box.

84
00:04:56,296 --> 00:05:00,008
[Dail] He was trying to pull me over
as hard as he could.

85
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:03,887
I knew we were going
to end up fighting from the get-go.

86
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:07,057
Still, I've worked out a lot,
so I felt confident.

87
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:13,271
[chain whirring]

88
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:17,192
YUK JUNSEO, PHYSICAL
FORMER UDT/SEAL, THE IRON SQUAD S1 WINNER

89
00:05:17,275 --> 00:05:20,737
I have a military background.

90
00:05:20,821 --> 00:05:23,073
And I enjoy physical training,

91
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:26,535
so I think I'd have an advantage
in any physical challenge.

92
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:29,830
Wait, Yuk Junseo is here.

93
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:34,876
He has clearly come prepared.
He's already in combat mode.

94
00:05:39,798 --> 00:05:42,467
[Junseo] I was confident
when it came to using strength.

95
00:05:43,552 --> 00:05:48,557
Yang Dail was behind me
and was stronger than I expected.

96
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:50,475
So I responded with my strength.

97
00:05:56,314 --> 00:05:57,566
[chain rattling]

98
00:05:57,649 --> 00:05:58,650
[gasps]

99
00:06:03,405 --> 00:06:05,156
[chain clinking]

100
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:11,997
[chain rattles]

101
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:18,879
No offense to Pani Bottle,
but I thought I could handle him.

102
00:06:18,962 --> 00:06:20,005
Wow.

103
00:06:20,672 --> 00:06:24,092
[Eunsil] I was the first one
to get the hint.

104
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:27,512
FIRST, SECOND, THIRD

105
00:06:29,389 --> 00:06:30,849
[host] Get rid of the first.

106
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:34,269
Cut off the heads of the seconds
and offer them on the altar.

107
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:40,025
[Junseo] I thought about
what it could mean.

108
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:42,527
[Dail] I found it really hard.

109
00:06:43,862 --> 00:06:45,822
The first's head...

110
00:06:45,906 --> 00:06:48,408
What did it say?
Something about cutting off a head

111
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:51,536
and cutting open the second's stomach
to make an offering.

112
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:53,747
I had no clue what it meant.

113
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:55,206
I really had no idea.

114
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,797
[Pani Bottle] I checked the hint
inside the box.

115
00:07:02,881 --> 00:07:07,135
The numbers and letters
kind of looked like 10, 20 and 30.

116
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:12,265
I tried different combinations,
but nothing worked.

117
00:07:12,349 --> 00:07:13,892
I wondered what it could be.

118
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:18,438
I thought I was prepared, so I was sure
that I'd solve the first puzzle.

119
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,023
But I was stuck.

120
00:07:20,607 --> 00:07:24,736
[Jieun] Since using my brain
isn't really my strong suit,

121
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:27,656
I've decided to solve things
with my physical strength.

122
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:29,240
[thudding]

123
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:38,708
The first's head...

124
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,671
[ZZONE] I felt like
the answer had to be there,

125
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:44,089
so I read it over and over.

126
00:07:44,631 --> 00:07:45,840
Wait a second.

127
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:49,636
BEWARE OF YOUR OPPONENT'S LIES
LEAVE YOUR SAFE HAVEN

128
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,304
THE TRUTH IS HIDDEN UNDERNEATH

129
00:07:51,388 --> 00:07:53,598
QUESTION FAKE OBEDIENCE
UNCOVER WHAT'S HIDDEN

130
00:07:53,682 --> 00:07:55,183
THE TRUTH IS HIDDEN UNDERNEATH

131
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:59,646
There were three lines of messages.

132
00:08:00,230 --> 00:08:03,525
I was sure they had something to do
with the answer.

133
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:08,947
I tried reading the messages.

134
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,700
When I read the characters
from top to bottom...

135
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:13,993
it said "under the mask."

136
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:18,289
UNDER THE MASK

137
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:21,084
"Under the chair" and "under the pillar."

138
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:23,962
So I looked under the mask...

139
00:08:24,963 --> 00:08:26,047
and there were numbers.

140
00:08:26,131 --> 00:08:27,424
FIRST, SECOND, THIRD

141
00:08:28,675 --> 00:08:30,093
[host] Get rid of the first.

142
00:08:31,261 --> 00:08:35,056
Cut off the heads of the seconds
and offer them on the altar.

143
00:08:36,599 --> 00:08:38,893
That is the key to your survival.

144
00:08:40,854 --> 00:08:43,189
UNDER THE CHAIR

145
00:08:44,149 --> 00:08:46,651
UNDER THE PILLAR

146
00:08:47,402 --> 00:08:50,572
UNDER THE MASK

147
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:52,115
[Jimin] I can't let them find out.

148
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:56,202
I was going to solve it and escape
while no one was watching.

149
00:09:01,624 --> 00:09:02,709
[lock clicking]

150
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,210
[clicks]

151
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:06,254
But it wouldn't work.

152
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:08,798
[groans] Seriously.

153
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,134
Come on. 3174...

154
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:13,219
That's when I started to panic.

155
00:09:13,303 --> 00:09:16,139
That had to be the answer,
but it wasn't working.

156
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,892
It was driving me crazy.

157
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:23,354
But I might have been entering
the code the wrong way.

158
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:25,774
It was the other way around.

159
00:09:29,152 --> 00:09:32,072
ENTERED THE CODE THE WRONG WAY

160
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,783
[host] You have three minutes left.

161
00:09:34,866 --> 00:09:36,785
REMAINING TIME

162
00:09:36,868 --> 00:09:38,787
[Jimin] The clock kept ticking.

163
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:40,580
This is driving me crazy.

164
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:42,749
What do I do?

165
00:09:46,211 --> 00:09:47,629
[cries]

166
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:49,380
What am I supposed to do?

167
00:09:49,464 --> 00:09:51,925
[footsteps]

168
00:09:53,134 --> 00:09:54,135
[Jimin] Wait...

169
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:55,929
Who's that?

170
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:59,349
[Jimin] Excuse me. Wait.

171
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:01,643
It's impossible. How did they do it?

172
00:10:07,524 --> 00:10:09,901
[Jimin] I was panicking
since I was completely stuck,

173
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:12,237
but people kept passing by.

174
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:14,364
[footsteps approaching]

175
00:10:14,447 --> 00:10:16,908
Excuse me.

176
00:10:24,207 --> 00:10:26,459
When I saw more people pass by,

177
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:29,170
I started getting really nervous.

178
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:32,632
How on earth did they get free?

179
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:38,096
It was tied to the belt,
so I just forced it with my strength.

180
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:39,597
It was tied down really tight.

181
00:10:39,681 --> 00:10:41,141
I decided to force it open.

182
00:10:41,224 --> 00:10:43,518
I was confident in my physical strength.

183
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:45,687
[Dail] I had to survive first.

184
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:48,356
PLAYERS WHO RELY ON PHYSICAL STRENGTH

185
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:50,859
-[Eunsil] Think it'll work?
-Yes, I think so.

186
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:53,361
-It's working. Just a little more...
-[Jieun laughing]

187
00:10:53,862 --> 00:10:55,864
-Got it!
-Thank you so much! It's finally off.

188
00:10:55,947 --> 00:10:57,407
-[Eunsil] Pants, pants.
-Okay.

189
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,951
Come on, hurry.

190
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:02,620
[Dail] You need help?

191
00:11:05,623 --> 00:11:07,917
[♪ playful music plays]

192
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:15,133
STAGGERS

193
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:18,303
It's coming off.

194
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:23,016
I figured I could get it off
by taking my pants off.

195
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:25,935
[ZZONE] I didn't want to be eliminated
on the first day.

196
00:11:26,019 --> 00:11:27,145
I pulled my belt down.

197
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:32,066
[♪ intriguing music playing]

198
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,282
[Eunsil] This is the Main Hall, right?

199
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,658
It's the Main Hall.

200
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:42,076
I think it is.

201
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:53,504
PLAYERS ARRIVE ONE BY ONE

202
00:11:55,298 --> 00:11:56,549
Hello.

203
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:57,967
Here.

204
00:11:58,051 --> 00:12:01,888
[Sanghyun] After about 10 minutes,
it seemed like everyone had arrived.

205
00:12:02,805 --> 00:12:04,849
[Eunsil] Then, I saw Yuk Junseo,

206
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:07,101
and I saw the baseball player.

207
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:10,438
Physical strength-wise, I thought,
"This isn't going to be easy."

208
00:12:11,272 --> 00:12:14,817
I didn't see anyone
who seemed particularly intimidating.

209
00:12:14,901 --> 00:12:16,861
I thought I might be weaker physically,

210
00:12:16,945 --> 00:12:20,698
but I could have a better chance
if there are games that use your brain.

211
00:12:21,950 --> 00:12:24,994
[Joonsu] I didn't want to team up
with Youn Sanghyun,

212
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:26,454
because his eyes looked suspicious.

213
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:29,207
Since he's an actor,
he'd be good at acting.

214
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:30,959
He seemed suspicious.

215
00:12:31,960 --> 00:12:33,670
My ear hurts. Damn it.

216
00:12:34,671 --> 00:12:36,381
Aren't there quite a few people

217
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,341
-who haven't arrived yet?
-Yes.

218
00:12:39,092 --> 00:12:40,677
Only one gets eliminated.

219
00:12:42,095 --> 00:12:44,555
[Sujin] I need to take off
this inner layer.

220
00:12:47,308 --> 00:12:48,768
This won't come off.

221
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:51,896
[groans]

222
00:12:52,522 --> 00:12:53,523
This is so annoying.

223
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:56,859
At that point, I wasn't even thinking
about solving the problem.

224
00:12:56,943 --> 00:12:58,278
I just panicked

225
00:12:58,361 --> 00:13:01,197
and started yanking them down
as hard as I could.

226
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:05,702
I'd do whatever it takes not to be last.

227
00:13:06,536 --> 00:13:07,745
[exhales]

228
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:09,998
[Sujin] Let's get out of here quickly.

229
00:13:10,081 --> 00:13:11,207
It won't be me.

230
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:13,167
It shouldn't be me.

231
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:17,338
-Damn it.
-[Sujin groans] My back hurts so bad.

232
00:13:17,422 --> 00:13:20,174
[ZZONE] I ended up
being the first one to get out.

233
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:22,468
Seriously, I debated what to do.

234
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:25,096
It's a survival game, after all.
So should I just go

235
00:13:25,179 --> 00:13:27,307
or help one of them get out?

236
00:13:29,767 --> 00:13:31,769
[♪ tense music playing]

237
00:13:37,817 --> 00:13:38,860
What do I do?

238
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:45,158
-Do you need help?
-[player breathes]

239
00:13:46,117 --> 00:13:47,827
ZZONE CHOOSES JIMIN

240
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:50,121
I'll hold onto my pants.
Can you pull it down?

241
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:53,166
[ZZONE] I think
you've pulled it down well.

242
00:13:53,875 --> 00:13:55,793
Just pull them down. Hold on.

243
00:13:55,877 --> 00:14:00,173
Jimin has experience
being on other reality survival programs.

244
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:03,342
So I figured I really shouldn't end up
as her enemy.

245
00:14:03,426 --> 00:14:06,012
It's all going to come off.
They're coming off.

246
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:09,515
It's because I took off my inner layer.

247
00:14:09,599 --> 00:14:10,600
[exhales]

248
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:12,310
-Wait.
-[ZZONE] Sorry?

249
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:13,978
-No, no.
-It's way too tight.

250
00:14:14,062 --> 00:14:16,314
Like this. This is way too tight.

251
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:17,440
[ZZONE] Right?

252
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,901
We can't be last though.

253
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:21,986
[♪ dramatic music playing]

254
00:14:29,035 --> 00:14:30,661
We really can't be last.

255
00:14:32,413 --> 00:14:34,082
[Sujin] Wow. [sniffles]

256
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:37,585
They wouldn't let me out.

257
00:14:38,169 --> 00:14:39,170
[exhales]

258
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,380
My back hurts.

259
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:42,965
[groans]

260
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:46,594
Jimin and the one on my left
were in a hurry to leave.

261
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,722
I was so annoyed.

262
00:14:51,349 --> 00:14:52,475
[groans]

263
00:14:55,103 --> 00:14:57,355
[exhales] I was so mad that I was like,

264
00:14:58,272 --> 00:15:00,733
"Fine, wait and see who wins in the end."

265
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:04,737
[mic feedback]

266
00:15:05,238 --> 00:15:07,532
[host] It's time to reveal the results.

267
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:11,035
In Deadly Tag...

268
00:15:12,829 --> 00:15:15,331
the player who finished last,
in 13th place...

269
00:15:15,957 --> 00:15:17,708
is Gyeong Sujin.

270
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:24,423
She will not be able to participate
in the first game, the Main Match.

271
00:15:24,966 --> 00:15:28,636
AN EMPTY SEAT

272
00:15:31,931 --> 00:15:34,016
[Eunsil] So this is how it starts.

273
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:39,105
[Jieun] To be honest,
I was glad I made it through.

274
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,733
[Joonsu] I felt bad for her
but was glad it wasn't me.

275
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:47,238
It's a survival program, after all.
I have to save myself first.

276
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:54,328
[host] Now, each player
will enter the Dealer Room

277
00:15:54,412 --> 00:15:57,081
and hand in your prize cards.

278
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:02,670
AFTER THE FIRST GAME

279
00:16:03,629 --> 00:16:04,630
[Horseking] What is this?

280
00:16:04,714 --> 00:16:05,840
CARDS IN THE MAIN HALL

281
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:06,924
[Joonsu] What are these?

282
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:12,805
PRIZE CARDS FOR EVERYONE WHO ESCAPED,
EXCEPT THE PLAYER IN 13TH PLACE

283
00:16:12,889 --> 00:16:16,684
100 MILLION, 80 MILLION WON,
60 MILLION, 40 MILLION, 20 MILLION WON

284
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:20,688
EXCHANGE THE PRIZE CARDS FOR CASH
IN THE DEALER ROOM

285
00:16:21,189 --> 00:16:24,317
DEPOSIT THE MONEY INTO THE LOCKERS

286
00:16:25,776 --> 00:16:27,028
-[dealer] Hello.
-Hello.

287
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:30,239
[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
please present your prize card.

288
00:16:34,869 --> 00:16:37,246
[Sanghyun] I got
to the Main Hall first, but...

289
00:16:38,039 --> 00:16:39,874
SECOND PLACE: JANG EUNSIL

290
00:16:42,585 --> 00:16:45,504
I was reading the instructions
about the cards,

291
00:16:45,588 --> 00:16:48,382
and then Jang Eunsil
took the 100 million won card

292
00:16:48,466 --> 00:16:49,508
before I did.

293
00:16:50,092 --> 00:16:52,762
So I went ahead and took
the 80 million won one.

294
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:55,848
[Eunsil] All I could see
was the 100 million won card,

295
00:16:55,932 --> 00:16:57,266
so I grabbed it.

296
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:58,351
What is this?

297
00:16:58,434 --> 00:17:04,857
[dealer] Please choose one key number
from 1 to 14 and state your choice.

298
00:17:04,941 --> 00:17:06,984
[Sanghyun] I'll go with number nine.

299
00:17:07,068 --> 00:17:09,820
YOUN SANGHYUN: 80 MILLION WON & KEY NO. 9

300
00:17:09,904 --> 00:17:12,698
You have selected key number one.

301
00:17:12,782 --> 00:17:15,576
Ms. Jang Eunsil's prize card
is 100 million won.

302
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,536
I'll go with number eight.

303
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:22,291
-Number five.
-[dealer] You've picked number five.

304
00:17:24,252 --> 00:17:27,046
Please deposit your personal funds
into the locker.

305
00:17:29,423 --> 00:17:32,385
ALL PLAYERS' FUNDS HAVE BEEN DEPOSITED

306
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,137
[Pani Bottle] Geez, what's going on?

307
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:39,058
[dealer] Please select a player.

308
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,434
[Ddolddol] What's this?

309
00:17:40,518 --> 00:17:43,437
-[ZZONE] This is driving me nuts.
-[Dail] God damn it.

310
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:46,274
-[Horseking] This is fun.
-[Sanghyun] It's me, right?

311
00:17:46,357 --> 00:17:48,484
[Joonsu] Hold on, I got betrayed.

312
00:17:50,278 --> 00:17:51,779
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

313
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:56,867
[host] To those who survived
the advantage game, congratulations.

314
00:17:56,951 --> 00:18:01,247
Here are the basic rules of Deadly Tag.

315
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:04,542
Deadly Tag will proceed
with the Death Match...

316
00:18:05,126 --> 00:18:07,920
after the Main Match
and a round of voting.

317
00:18:08,004 --> 00:18:10,089
Players who place last in each Main Match

318
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:13,593
or those who do not earn
an Elimination Immunity Pass

319
00:18:13,676 --> 00:18:15,386
will be at risk of elimination.

320
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:20,057
The final Death Match player
will be decided by voting.

321
00:18:20,141 --> 00:18:24,854
The Death Match result
will determine who is eliminated.

322
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:27,690
The final survivor of Deadly Tag

323
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:31,360
will receive the grand prize
of 100 million won.

324
00:18:32,653 --> 00:18:35,197
[Junseo] I wanted to win it,
and I know I can.

325
00:18:35,281 --> 00:18:37,116
[Sanghyun] The prize money matters,

326
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,744
but there's also the thrill, the honor,

327
00:18:39,827 --> 00:18:42,163
and the pride that come with winning.

328
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,040
[Dail] My goal? To win.

329
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:45,916
I'll destroy everybody.

330
00:18:47,168 --> 00:18:49,712
[host] The first Main Match
of Deadly Tag is...

331
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:55,718
"Cops and Robbers."

332
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:58,554
C&R.

333
00:18:58,638 --> 00:18:59,972
Wow.

334
00:19:00,056 --> 00:19:01,057
What?

335
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:02,767
[host] Cops and Robbers

336
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:07,521
consists of three cops and nine robbers
with each player taking a role.

337
00:19:07,605 --> 00:19:09,231
Cops are split into three roles.

338
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:12,026
Criminal Investigation,
Violent Crimes, and Narcotics.

339
00:19:12,109 --> 00:19:13,611
Robbers are split into groups of three.

340
00:19:13,694 --> 00:19:17,239
Burglars, Assault Criminals,
and Drug Criminals.

341
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:18,616
CI will handle Burglars,

342
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:20,326
Violent Crimes
will handle Assault Criminals,

343
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:23,204
and Narcotics will handle Drug Criminals.

344
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:27,291
Players start the game
without knowing each other's identities.

345
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,044
The chase consists of two rounds,

346
00:19:30,127 --> 00:19:34,131
and each round includes
a chase and an interrogation.

347
00:19:34,215 --> 00:19:39,595
Criminals must collect
a set number of clues during the chase,

348
00:19:39,679 --> 00:19:43,683
and if they fail to do so, a regular clue
and a decisive clue about that criminal

349
00:19:43,766 --> 00:19:46,894
will be randomly revealed to all players.

350
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:52,024
During the chase,
cops can tag up to three criminals.

351
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:55,403
Tagged criminals are locked up in prison.

352
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:58,906
There are special roles
hidden among the criminals.

353
00:19:58,989 --> 00:20:03,077
The Good Citizen
helps the cop handling their case

354
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,704
catch the other criminals.

355
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:07,790
There are two Good Citizens,

356
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:11,794
with one each
in two of the criminal groups.

357
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:16,132
The Madman
wants to be caught by the police

358
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:18,884
and lures their assigned cop
into capturing them.

359
00:20:19,969 --> 00:20:23,597
There is one Madman in the criminal group
without a Good Citizen.

360
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:27,309
After both chase rounds,
the cops and criminals

361
00:20:27,393 --> 00:20:31,731
will vote to arrest a criminal
and identify a traitor respectively.

362
00:20:31,814 --> 00:20:35,651
Once a cop locks up
both of their assigned criminals,

363
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:37,069
their mission is complete.

364
00:20:37,611 --> 00:20:42,408
But if a Good Citizen or the Madman
is among them, their mission fails.

365
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:46,287
If a criminal avoids getting arrested
by their assigned cop...

366
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:50,541
or if they successfully identify
a Good Citizen or the Madman

367
00:20:50,624 --> 00:20:52,084
in the vote to find traitors,

368
00:20:52,168 --> 00:20:53,502
their mission is complete.

369
00:20:54,003 --> 00:20:57,673
The Good Citizens win if they survive
the criminals' vote to find traitors

370
00:20:57,757 --> 00:21:02,678
and if their assigned cop arrests
the two other criminals on their team.

371
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:06,140
The Madman wins if they survive
the criminals' vote to find traitors

372
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:09,560
and if they get arrested
by their assigned cop.

373
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:14,273
Those who complete their missions
will earn 20 million won

374
00:21:14,356 --> 00:21:16,859
and one Elimination Immunity Pass.

375
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:19,820
Those who fail their missions

376
00:21:19,904 --> 00:21:23,824
will be subject to an Elimination Vote
to decide two elimination candidates.

377
00:21:25,201 --> 00:21:26,285
What?

378
00:21:27,661 --> 00:21:28,996
[Junseo] This is not easy.

379
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:30,998
This seems pretty intricate.

380
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:33,375
-Cops...
-Three cops and nine criminals.

381
00:21:33,459 --> 00:21:35,252
Among the criminals...

382
00:21:35,336 --> 00:21:38,589
There are two Good Citizens
and one Madman.

383
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:40,800
There's one hidden in each group.

384
00:21:40,883 --> 00:21:43,636
-It's like the game Mafia.
-[ZZONE] Yeah, it feels like that.

385
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:46,889
The Good Citizens could help the cops out.

386
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:49,183
Exactly, Good Citizens have to help
to win.

387
00:21:49,266 --> 00:21:50,351
I see.

388
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:52,686
Catch the criminals
and avoid being voted out.

389
00:21:52,770 --> 00:21:54,647
I think it's the most difficult role.

390
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:59,527
There's no doubt the cops need
speed and physical strength.

391
00:21:59,610 --> 00:22:03,823
As for these criminals and special roles,

392
00:22:03,906 --> 00:22:08,619
they could still deceive people
if they can put on a good act.

393
00:22:08,702 --> 00:22:12,081
The criminals have to find their clues
and keep them hidden.

394
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:14,625
So they need to use
their bodies and brains.

395
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:16,460
I thought observation was the key.

396
00:22:16,544 --> 00:22:19,713
Not just observing the clues
but also observing people.

397
00:22:19,797 --> 00:22:21,799
The most important thing is tackling.

398
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:26,303
I absolutely knew I had to get physical.

399
00:22:26,387 --> 00:22:27,805
So, I was quite confident.

400
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:31,934
[host] Now, each player will enter
the Dealer Room one by one

401
00:22:32,017 --> 00:22:35,521
and draw a role card
for the Cops and Robbers game.

402
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:43,821
[Ddolddol]
I didn't really want to be a cop

403
00:22:43,904 --> 00:22:45,948
because I felt like

404
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:49,034
the role would involve
a lot of hands-on fighting

405
00:22:49,118 --> 00:22:50,327
and physical clashes.

406
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:54,248
-Hello.
-Mr. Kim Ddolddol,

407
00:22:54,331 --> 00:22:56,375
please point to one card of your choice.

408
00:22:58,586 --> 00:23:00,588
[♪ mysterious music playing]

409
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:05,759
[Ddolddol] This one.

410
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:09,805
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol,

411
00:23:09,889 --> 00:23:11,307
you are Robber 2.

412
00:23:11,974 --> 00:23:13,058
Also...

413
00:23:14,310 --> 00:23:15,603
you are a Good Citizen.

414
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:21,025
You need to help the cops
catch the other criminals

415
00:23:21,108 --> 00:23:24,278
and survive the criminals' vote
to find traitors.

416
00:23:25,029 --> 00:23:28,574
[Ddolddol] The moment I drew the card,
I thought it was perfect for me.

417
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:29,825
Even when I play Mafia,

418
00:23:29,909 --> 00:23:32,369
I'm really good at special roles,
like the shaman.

419
00:23:32,453 --> 00:23:33,829
I'm always good at those roles.

420
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:37,041
I'll go straight to the police
and sell out the criminals' info.

421
00:23:37,124 --> 00:23:40,085
I'll also figure out
who are the other criminals on my team

422
00:23:40,169 --> 00:23:43,547
and act like I'm not the traitor.

423
00:23:43,631 --> 00:23:45,966
[dealer] Here's your profile card
and notebook.

424
00:23:46,050 --> 00:23:47,676
PROFILE CARDS LIST THE CRIME & CLUES

425
00:23:55,684 --> 00:23:57,227
[all chuckle]

426
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:05,778
Excuse me, can I ask what you picked?

427
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:07,571
I'm the one being chased.

428
00:24:08,322 --> 00:24:09,657
I'll run for my life.

429
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:12,576
Hello.

430
00:24:14,036 --> 00:24:16,705
Mr. Lee Joonsu,
please point to a card of your choice.

431
00:24:16,789 --> 00:24:18,791
[Joonsu] I wanted to be a cop.

432
00:24:18,874 --> 00:24:21,168
Horseking and Yuk Junseo...

433
00:24:21,251 --> 00:24:23,837
Except for those two,
I can catch everyone else.

434
00:24:23,921 --> 00:24:25,047
Mr. Lee Joonsu...

435
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,508
you are Robber 3.

436
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:30,177
And you are a regular criminal.

437
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:33,097
[Joonsu] I'm glad I wasn't a Good Citizen
or the Madman.

438
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:35,015
A regular criminal is simple and nice.

439
00:24:35,099 --> 00:24:39,228
[Pani Bottle] I was hoping to get
either the Good Citizen or the Madman.

440
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:42,898
I thought the Madman role
would be easier to play.

441
00:24:42,982 --> 00:24:46,402
I figured if I just did my best,
the criminals would identify me.

442
00:24:46,986 --> 00:24:49,488
[Jimin] Since I'm pretty good at acting,

443
00:24:49,571 --> 00:24:51,865
I thought I could do the Madman role.

444
00:24:51,949 --> 00:24:53,450
[dealer] Mr. Pani Bottle...

445
00:24:53,534 --> 00:24:55,869
you are Assault Criminal 1.

446
00:24:55,953 --> 00:24:57,746
You are [bleep].

447
00:24:58,872 --> 00:25:01,792
Ms. Park Jimin, you are Drug Criminal 2.

448
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:03,419
You are [bleep].

449
00:25:10,384 --> 00:25:11,885
[Horseking] I'll go with this one.

450
00:25:11,969 --> 00:25:13,262
[dealer] Mr. Horseking...

451
00:25:13,971 --> 00:25:15,889
you are Assault Criminal 2.

452
00:25:15,973 --> 00:25:17,766
You are [bleep].

453
00:25:18,851 --> 00:25:21,437
Mr. Yang Dail, you are [bleep].

454
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:29,778
Those are your clues?

455
00:25:29,862 --> 00:25:30,904
-Yes.
-I see.

456
00:25:30,988 --> 00:25:33,615
-It includes photos and locations.
-[Dail] I see.

457
00:25:33,699 --> 00:25:36,201
So you have to find and get rid of them?

458
00:25:36,285 --> 00:25:39,538
[host] The chase area is divided
into four sections.

459
00:25:40,789 --> 00:25:41,790
The Hotel,

460
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:43,542
the Grounds,

461
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:45,461
the Pool,

462
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:47,963
and the Annex.

463
00:25:49,882 --> 00:25:52,843
Each criminal
must collect nine physical clues

464
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:55,387
placed throughout the chase area.

465
00:25:55,471 --> 00:25:57,931
The clues consist
of seven general clues...

466
00:25:58,724 --> 00:26:02,644
and two decisive clues
that easily help identify the criminal.

467
00:26:03,228 --> 00:26:07,191
The criminals can locate the clues
using the provided photos.

468
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:12,071
FIND THE LOCATIONS IN THE PHOTOS
AND PICK UP THE CLUES

469
00:26:14,698 --> 00:26:16,700
[♪ intriguing music playing]

470
00:26:17,326 --> 00:26:19,495
Wait, they zoomed in way too much.

471
00:26:20,621 --> 00:26:23,082
-How am I supposed to find these?
-You can't show them.

472
00:26:23,165 --> 00:26:24,374
How can I find them?

473
00:26:24,458 --> 00:26:26,126
Are you the Madman?

474
00:26:26,210 --> 00:26:27,294
[all laughing]

475
00:26:27,377 --> 00:26:28,629
[Jieun] Right. [chuckles]

476
00:26:33,926 --> 00:26:35,886
[♪ intriguing music playing]

477
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:41,433
Be careful.

478
00:26:41,517 --> 00:26:43,268
Yuk Junseo is a cop.

479
00:26:43,352 --> 00:26:44,645
Are you a cop?

480
00:26:44,728 --> 00:26:45,938
Yes.

481
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:48,023
[♪ powerful music playing]

482
00:26:48,899 --> 00:26:50,359
[Jaegyun] Here comes the UDT.

483
00:26:50,442 --> 00:26:51,443
[Ddolddol groans]

484
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,363
[dealer] Mr. Yuk Junseo...

485
00:26:56,156 --> 00:26:57,825
you are a Violent Crimes cop.

486
00:26:59,576 --> 00:27:02,204
Here's your profile card
and investigation notebook.

487
00:27:03,789 --> 00:27:05,874
This is exactly the scenario in my head

488
00:27:05,958 --> 00:27:10,003
where I really hoped the cops
wouldn't be like someone like him.

489
00:27:10,087 --> 00:27:11,672
[all laugh]

490
00:27:16,677 --> 00:27:19,054
-You're a cop, right?
-[Sanghyun] Are you a cop?

491
00:27:19,138 --> 00:27:21,348
[Jaegyun] It's so easy to tell
who's a cop or robber.

492
00:27:21,431 --> 00:27:23,725
I guess the cops get those notebooks.

493
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:26,061
[Ddolddol] Cops get notebooks.

494
00:27:27,396 --> 00:27:32,734
AN INVESTIGATION NOTEBOOK
WITH PROFILES OF ALL THE CRIMINALS

495
00:27:32,818 --> 00:27:36,280
[dealer] Mr. Youn Sanghyun,
you are a Criminal Investigation cop.

496
00:27:36,363 --> 00:27:37,573
Okay.

497
00:27:38,699 --> 00:27:40,325
[dealer] Ms. Jang Eunsil...

498
00:27:40,409 --> 00:27:42,494
you are a Narcotics cop.

499
00:27:43,412 --> 00:27:44,413
Okay.

500
00:27:44,496 --> 00:27:46,915
As soon as I got the role,
I thought it was a perfect fit for me.

501
00:27:46,999 --> 00:27:51,670
You need the stamina to pull off the role,

502
00:27:51,753 --> 00:27:54,131
so it was something
I felt confident about.

503
00:27:56,216 --> 00:27:58,719
[Jieun] The cop roles
went to people who fit them.

504
00:27:58,802 --> 00:28:00,721
-[Jimin] I know.
-[Sanghyun] Honestly,

505
00:28:00,804 --> 00:28:04,766
Junseo and Eunsil
are both fit and athletic, so I thought

506
00:28:04,850 --> 00:28:06,518
I got lucky with our team.

507
00:28:06,602 --> 00:28:09,897
And Sanghyun seemed like
someone who's pretty sharp.

508
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:15,444
As a Good Citizen,
I was very happy with the cops.

509
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:18,196
CI: SANGHYUN,
VIOLENT CRIMES: JUNSEO, NARCOTICS: EUNSIL

510
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:20,991
SHIN JIEUN, HWANG JAEGYUN, YANG DAIL:
UNKNOWN

511
00:28:21,074 --> 00:28:23,035
[♪ exciting music playing]

512
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:37,841
[host] In Cops and Robbers,
here's how the tag system works.

513
00:28:38,342 --> 00:28:41,762
At the start, cops have blue patches,

514
00:28:41,845 --> 00:28:44,514
and criminals wear red patches.

515
00:28:45,557 --> 00:28:48,518
If a cop completely removes
a criminal's patch,

516
00:28:48,602 --> 00:28:50,187
it counts as a tag.

517
00:28:51,229 --> 00:28:56,109
You'll now have 20 minutes
for Round 1 private discussions.

518
00:28:57,361 --> 00:29:02,783
ROUND 1 PRIVATE TALKS FOR CRIMINALS

519
00:29:02,866 --> 00:29:05,243
LOOKING AROUND

520
00:29:06,662 --> 00:29:09,373
CRIMINALS HESITATE TO SAY ANYTHING

521
00:29:09,957 --> 00:29:11,959
-You're a criminal?
-I am.

522
00:29:12,042 --> 00:29:14,294
What kind? Assault?

523
00:29:14,378 --> 00:29:16,004
-What kind?
-Assault or...

524
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:17,422
Assault?

525
00:29:17,506 --> 00:29:20,300
-[Ddolddol] There are three groups.
-The three groups?

526
00:29:20,384 --> 00:29:25,180
Do we need to reveal that now?
Are you all willing to share your roles?

527
00:29:25,806 --> 00:29:27,182
[chuckles]

528
00:29:29,142 --> 00:29:31,269
Unless you're a Good Citizen
or the Madman,

529
00:29:31,353 --> 00:29:32,604
it's better to share.

530
00:29:32,688 --> 00:29:34,815
[♪ tense music playing]

531
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:40,946
Do we need to reveal them?
I don't see why...

532
00:29:41,029 --> 00:29:43,198
It's easier to catch traitors if we do.

533
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:46,451
As a criminal, you have to be prepared
in case you get caught.

534
00:29:46,535 --> 00:29:50,122
After being caught, the way to survive
is to identify the Good Citizens.

535
00:29:50,205 --> 00:29:54,376
And to do that,
we need to know who's on which team,

536
00:29:54,459 --> 00:29:57,462
so we can narrow them down.

537
00:29:58,755 --> 00:30:00,841
-That's true, but--
-If someone hesitates,

538
00:30:00,924 --> 00:30:03,552
they're either a Good Citizen
or the Madman.

539
00:30:06,638 --> 00:30:08,557
[Dail] Even if we get arrested
by the cops,

540
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:10,475
we can survive as long as we find

541
00:30:10,559 --> 00:30:13,145
the Good Citizen
or the Madman on our teams.

542
00:30:13,228 --> 00:30:16,481
You just need to be good
at finding clues and reading people.

543
00:30:16,565 --> 00:30:19,109
Constantly running away isn't the key.

544
00:30:19,192 --> 00:30:21,778
That could actually backfire too.

545
00:30:22,362 --> 00:30:25,073
If I reveal which team I'm on,

546
00:30:25,157 --> 00:30:27,492
and the Madman happens to be

547
00:30:27,576 --> 00:30:28,994
-on my team...
-Exactly.

548
00:30:29,077 --> 00:30:32,581
If we discuss altogether,
the lies will come out.

549
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:35,792
We'll end up with a higher number
of criminals if someone lies.

550
00:30:36,585 --> 00:30:38,378
[Ddolddol] He cut me off.

551
00:30:38,462 --> 00:30:40,505
I was so annoyed. [scoffs]

552
00:30:40,589 --> 00:30:44,217
Am I going to get identified by Yang Dail?

553
00:30:45,010 --> 00:30:47,929
-[Horseking] Then, should we share--
-It's easier if we do.

554
00:30:49,181 --> 00:30:50,223
Is that so?

555
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:55,062
[ZZONE] It could work out, but what if
there's a Good Citizen on our team?

556
00:30:55,145 --> 00:30:58,398
We could be doomed, right?
If I share which team I'm on,

557
00:30:59,066 --> 00:31:01,693
and a Good Citizen tells on me...

558
00:31:01,777 --> 00:31:06,073
Exactly, but Dail wants everyone
to reveal their roles.

559
00:31:06,156 --> 00:31:07,407
[ZZONE] Yeah, I know.

560
00:31:08,033 --> 00:31:11,953
[Pani Bottle] I'm a little confused.
Then, when the cops make an arrest,

561
00:31:12,037 --> 00:31:14,164
do they have to guess
both their role and crime?

562
00:31:14,247 --> 00:31:16,208
-Yes.
-If it's the right role but wrong crime,

563
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:17,292
-that won't count?
-No.

564
00:31:17,375 --> 00:31:20,295
I think the criminals might be better off

565
00:31:20,378 --> 00:31:23,006
not sharing that information
with each other.

566
00:31:23,090 --> 00:31:24,299
[ZZONE] Because there are Good Citizens.

567
00:31:24,382 --> 00:31:26,718
[Pani Bottle] If they don't get
the crime right,

568
00:31:26,802 --> 00:31:28,178
the cops can't make an arrest.

569
00:31:28,261 --> 00:31:30,222
Sharing makes it easier
for Good Citizens to rat.

570
00:31:30,305 --> 00:31:32,349
That's how I see it too.

571
00:31:32,432 --> 00:31:34,184
We have two rounds anyway.

572
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:36,520
[Jieun] Let's not share for Round 1.

573
00:31:37,729 --> 00:31:40,524
[Dail] I was so frustrated
to see that happen.

574
00:31:40,607 --> 00:31:42,067
I think this private discussion time

575
00:31:42,150 --> 00:31:44,736
is the first and only opportunity
to figure out

576
00:31:44,820 --> 00:31:47,155
who the Good Citizens are
and who the Madman is

577
00:31:47,239 --> 00:31:51,660
by reading people's subtle hints
and reactions.

578
00:31:51,743 --> 00:31:54,496
But nobody was willing
to share their roles.

579
00:31:57,958 --> 00:31:59,459
Since no one said anything...

580
00:32:00,961 --> 00:32:01,962
I just watched.

581
00:32:10,095 --> 00:32:11,221
[mic feedback]

582
00:32:11,304 --> 00:32:15,392
[host] We will now begin Round 1
of the chase.

583
00:32:16,143 --> 00:32:17,853
[alarm blaring]

584
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:21,189
ROUND 1 CHASE

585
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:22,274
Darn it.

586
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:24,025
[Joonsu] Where do we go?

587
00:32:24,109 --> 00:32:25,402
FIND 4 CLUES AND AVOID ARREST

588
00:32:25,485 --> 00:32:27,571
[Ddolddol] Even with all the clues,
we can't get caught?

589
00:32:27,654 --> 00:32:31,241
-[Joonsu] Right, you can't get caught.
-[ZZONE] Geez, I am scared to death!

590
00:32:31,825 --> 00:32:34,411
-[Jieun] Is this the Pool?
-[Dail] How do we get in?

591
00:32:34,494 --> 00:32:36,037
[Jieun] Beats me. Just go.

592
00:32:36,580 --> 00:32:39,249
THE POOL

593
00:32:39,332 --> 00:32:41,334
[♪ powerful music playing]

594
00:32:42,878 --> 00:32:43,879
[sniffles]

595
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:45,422
[Pani Bottle] Is it this way?

596
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:55,515
The dirt pile. Where is it?

597
00:32:57,601 --> 00:32:58,810
There's no time.

598
00:33:00,312 --> 00:33:05,317
I figured I should start with the Pool
since it was the farthest from us.

599
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:08,945
So I gathered all the pool photos together
and headed there.

600
00:33:10,864 --> 00:33:11,990
What the fuck is this?

601
00:33:12,073 --> 00:33:13,658
YANG DAIL'S PHOTO OF CLUE LOCATION

602
00:33:15,076 --> 00:33:18,288
SEARCHING FOR THE DIRT PILE
THAT MATCHES THE PHOTO

603
00:33:24,461 --> 00:33:25,629
Where is this place?

604
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:27,547
HOWEVER THE CLUE IS NOWHERE TO BE SEEN

605
00:33:31,509 --> 00:33:32,928
Where is this?

606
00:33:35,722 --> 00:33:40,018
THE POOL AREA IS1,000 PYEONG,
OR 3,300 SQUARE METERS

607
00:33:40,644 --> 00:33:42,270
[ZZONE] Why is the pool so huge?

608
00:33:42,938 --> 00:33:47,359
EVERYTHING IN SIGHT
IS WITHIN THE SEARCH AREA

609
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:51,446
Fuck, it's supposed to be here.

610
00:33:51,529 --> 00:33:54,407
It's not here on site.
What the heck is this?

611
00:33:55,492 --> 00:33:57,035
[ZZONE] Damn it, where is it?

612
00:33:59,579 --> 00:34:00,789
I'm right here though.

613
00:34:00,872 --> 00:34:02,874
THE ANNEX

614
00:34:03,875 --> 00:34:05,252
You can't find it, can you?

615
00:34:05,335 --> 00:34:06,628
This is the right place.

616
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:07,963
I know.

617
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:10,924
It was in the photo
but it wasn't at the place.

618
00:34:11,007 --> 00:34:13,260
Time was ticking,
and the cops were about to come.

619
00:34:13,343 --> 00:34:14,803
And I totally panicked.

620
00:34:15,512 --> 00:34:16,513
THE GROUNDS

621
00:34:16,596 --> 00:34:19,015
What's this? Is this it? No, it's not.

622
00:34:20,141 --> 00:34:23,812
THE POOL

623
00:34:23,895 --> 00:34:25,230
This is all there is.

624
00:34:28,149 --> 00:34:29,567
Is it even here?

625
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:34,906
-You found one?
-Yes.

626
00:34:34,990 --> 00:34:36,157
What does it look like?

627
00:34:36,825 --> 00:34:37,826
How did you find it?

628
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:39,828
I looked at the photo.

629
00:34:39,911 --> 00:34:40,912
[exhales]

630
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:46,918
-How many did you find?
-[Jaegyun] Three.

631
00:34:47,002 --> 00:34:48,003
[Dail] Damn it.

632
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:50,630
[♪ energetic music playing]

633
00:34:55,343 --> 00:34:58,680
[Jaegyun] I'd already found everything
before the cops came out.

634
00:34:58,763 --> 00:35:01,182
I checked the notebook and the map

635
00:35:01,266 --> 00:35:04,936
to plan out the best route ahead of time.

636
00:35:06,938 --> 00:35:07,939
[beeps]

637
00:35:10,358 --> 00:35:11,359
[beeps]

638
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:12,819
-[Jimin] You found it?
-Yes.

639
00:35:13,695 --> 00:35:14,696
[beeps]

640
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:16,364
-[Joonsu] You found one?
-Yes.

641
00:35:16,448 --> 00:35:17,449
[beeps]

642
00:35:18,450 --> 00:35:20,619
I found everything really fast.

643
00:35:20,702 --> 00:35:23,330
I don't get why they can't find
what's in the photos.

644
00:35:24,289 --> 00:35:26,124
[Dail] Damn it,
I looked around here earlier.

645
00:35:26,207 --> 00:35:27,334
A MINUTE BEFORE THE COPS ENTER

646
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:31,755
I found it. I found it.

647
00:35:31,838 --> 00:35:33,256
I fucking found it.

648
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:35,175
I found it.

649
00:35:37,177 --> 00:35:38,178
[exhales]

650
00:35:38,261 --> 00:35:41,306
AFTER GETTING USED TO THE AREA,
THEY START FINDING THE CLUES

651
00:35:43,141 --> 00:35:45,602
HORSEKING COLLECTS A CLUE

652
00:35:46,519 --> 00:35:49,230
AND GETS RID OF THE PHOTO

653
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:52,108
[loud buzzer sounding]

654
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:53,860
[gasps]

655
00:35:54,611 --> 00:35:55,612
[groans]

656
00:35:57,322 --> 00:35:58,573
STARTLED

657
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:01,743
Fuck.

658
00:36:04,329 --> 00:36:06,456
[host] Cops may enter the chase area.

659
00:36:06,539 --> 00:36:07,540
COPS AND ROBBERS ROUND 1

660
00:36:07,624 --> 00:36:08,625
[shushes]

661
00:36:15,924 --> 00:36:19,386
YOUN SANGHYUN GOES ALONE
IN A DIFFERENT DIRECTION

662
00:36:23,515 --> 00:36:25,517
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

663
00:36:37,445 --> 00:36:39,364
-[Joonsu] What was that?
-They're on their way now.

664
00:36:39,447 --> 00:36:41,324
-The seekers are on the move.
-[Joonsu] Really?

665
00:36:41,950 --> 00:36:44,911
They'll come running.
This is connected to the outside.

666
00:36:44,994 --> 00:36:46,121
Keep your guard up.

667
00:36:46,746 --> 00:36:48,748
[footsteps]

668
00:36:51,751 --> 00:36:53,086
[gasps]

669
00:36:54,212 --> 00:36:56,005
COP SANGHYUN APPEARS

670
00:36:58,675 --> 00:36:59,676
[gasps]

671
00:37:01,511 --> 00:37:03,179
Hey, go that way. That way.

672
00:37:06,391 --> 00:37:08,601
THE CRIMINALS SCRAMBLE AS A COP APPEARS

673
00:37:15,817 --> 00:37:18,653
[Sanghyun] I checked
where the criminals were headed to

674
00:37:18,737 --> 00:37:21,573
before the cops started moving.

675
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:23,074
[♪ exciting music playing]

676
00:37:23,158 --> 00:37:24,492
EARLIER

677
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,873
[Junseo] As it's a wide area to cover,

678
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:33,168
I thought it'd be inefficient to move
as a group of three.

679
00:37:33,251 --> 00:37:35,962
I figure it'll take a while
to get familiar with the layout.

680
00:37:36,045 --> 00:37:37,797
-[Eunsil] So we split up?
-For Round 1, yes.

681
00:37:38,423 --> 00:37:41,926
[Sanghyun] I was in charge of the Pool
so I went down to my section.

682
00:37:42,010 --> 00:37:44,179
And there was a tall guy there.

683
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:48,600
He was looking around,
and then he started running in panic.

684
00:37:49,100 --> 00:37:50,477
I had to catch him.

685
00:37:51,478 --> 00:37:53,480
[♪ exciting music continues playing]

686
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:09,287
I used to run relay races
in elementary and middle school.

687
00:38:09,370 --> 00:38:10,413
I'm good at running.

688
00:38:15,627 --> 00:38:18,296
[Joonsu panting]

689
00:38:20,507 --> 00:38:22,175
-He got caught.
-He got him.

690
00:38:22,258 --> 00:38:24,135
[both panting]

691
00:38:29,557 --> 00:38:30,558
[grunts]

692
00:38:30,642 --> 00:38:32,644
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

693
00:38:32,727 --> 00:38:34,354
They're getting rough.

694
00:38:34,437 --> 00:38:35,438
[gasps]

695
00:38:36,314 --> 00:38:37,774
[both breathing heavily]

696
00:38:37,857 --> 00:38:41,194
[Sanghyun] Joonsu is 194 centimeters tall.

697
00:38:41,277 --> 00:38:42,821
[Joonsu] I was out of breath.

698
00:38:43,404 --> 00:38:45,365
I decided to confront him head on.

699
00:38:47,450 --> 00:38:50,203
[panting]

700
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:57,001
Physically, I'm quite tall.

701
00:38:57,085 --> 00:38:58,878
I have the edge over most people.

702
00:38:58,962 --> 00:39:02,048
[Sanghyun] Joonsu got a hold of me
and wouldn't let go.

703
00:39:02,131 --> 00:39:03,967
We went around in circles.

704
00:39:04,509 --> 00:39:07,679
I figured I'd get him from this side
with my left hand.

705
00:39:10,723 --> 00:39:12,976
LEE JOONSU LOSES HIS BALANCE

706
00:39:18,731 --> 00:39:20,817
JOONSU'S DESPERATE STRUGGLE

707
00:39:22,318 --> 00:39:23,486
[Joonsu groans]

708
00:39:25,405 --> 00:39:27,198
[both panting heavily]

709
00:39:27,282 --> 00:39:28,449
[patch rips]

710
00:39:28,533 --> 00:39:29,534
[exhales heavily]

711
00:39:30,660 --> 00:39:31,786
[host] Tag confirmed.

712
00:39:31,870 --> 00:39:32,871
SANGHYUN TAGS JOONSU

713
00:39:32,954 --> 00:39:33,955
[panting]

714
00:39:34,664 --> 00:39:35,707
[exhales]

715
00:39:35,790 --> 00:39:37,917
[panting heavily]

716
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:41,296
He's so strong.

717
00:39:42,255 --> 00:39:43,256
Wow.

718
00:39:45,008 --> 00:39:46,593
[host] Tag confirmed.

719
00:39:49,512 --> 00:39:50,805
[Ddolddol] Either way...

720
00:39:51,431 --> 00:39:56,477
I was going to go straight to the cops
and let myself get caught.

721
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:58,062
What's going on?

722
00:39:58,146 --> 00:39:59,147
LOOKING AROUND

723
00:40:00,189 --> 00:40:03,151
SPOTS A COP PASS BY FROM AFAR

724
00:40:05,904 --> 00:40:08,072
PRETENDS TO LOOK FOR CLUES

725
00:40:12,160 --> 00:40:13,161
There it is.

726
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:17,707
[patch rips]

727
00:40:17,790 --> 00:40:19,584
[host] Tag confirmed.

728
00:40:19,667 --> 00:40:20,710
What the heck?

729
00:40:20,793 --> 00:40:21,920
SANGHYUN TAGS DDOLDDOL

730
00:40:22,003 --> 00:40:23,087
[laughing]

731
00:40:23,171 --> 00:40:25,381
-Junseo!
-What the heck?

732
00:40:25,465 --> 00:40:27,508
-[Joonsu] I won't be lonely.
-[Ddolddol groans]

733
00:40:28,134 --> 00:40:30,511
I was right here. Mine was right here.

734
00:40:30,595 --> 00:40:31,596
DDOLDDOL KEEPS UP HIS ACT

735
00:40:32,931 --> 00:40:35,475
[Sanghyun] He clearly knew I was a cop,

736
00:40:35,558 --> 00:40:37,977
but he didn't resist
and let himself get caught.

737
00:40:38,061 --> 00:40:40,939
I wondered why he didn't run away.

738
00:40:41,022 --> 00:40:43,191
That seemed a little suspicious.

739
00:40:43,274 --> 00:40:44,984
[Joonsu] Which team are you on?

740
00:40:45,068 --> 00:40:47,487
-Burglars.
-Me too.

741
00:40:47,570 --> 00:40:49,072
Are you really a Burglar?

742
00:40:49,155 --> 00:40:52,033
Joonsu told me he was a Burglar too.

743
00:40:52,116 --> 00:40:53,618
I thought it was perfect.

744
00:40:53,701 --> 00:40:56,829
I figured I could use him
as my informant. [chuckles]

745
00:40:56,913 --> 00:40:58,164
-Did you see a fan here?
-No.

746
00:40:58,247 --> 00:40:59,749
GOOD CITIZEN APPROACHES WHILE DISGUISED

747
00:40:59,832 --> 00:41:00,833
The fan was right there.

748
00:41:00,917 --> 00:41:02,460
